prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method best_time_to_buy_and_sell_stock(prices: array<int>) returns (max_profit: int)
    requires 1 <= prices.Length <= 100000
    requires forall i :: 0 <= i < prices.Length ==> 0 <= prices[i] <= 10000
    ensures forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < prices.Length ==> max_profit >= prices[j] - prices[i]
{
    var min_price := 10001;
    max_profit := 0;

    var i := 0;
    while (i < prices.Length)
        invariant 0 <= i <= prices.Length
        invariant forall j :: 0 <= j < (i) - 1 ==> min_price <= prices[j]
        invariant forall j, k :: 0 <= j < k < i ==> max_profit >= prices[k] - prices[j]
    {
        var price := prices[i];
        if (price < min_price)
        {
            min_price := price;
        }
        if (price - min_price > max_profit) {
            max_profit := price - min_price;
        }

        i := i + 1;
    }
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(12,18): Error: this invariant could not be proved to be maintained by the loop
 Related message: loop invariant violation

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 1 error

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
At initial state: prices.Length = 5922, prices[5920] = 7002, prices[5921] = 7003. At a program state: min_price = 10001. At a program state: max_profit = 0. At a program state: i = 0.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

raw_response:
{
  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "preservation",
  "diagnosis": "The invariant `forall j :: 0 <= j < (i) - 1 ==> min_price <= prices[j]` has an off-by-one bound: it excludes index `i-1`. During loop preservation, after incrementing `i`, it needs to cover the element just processed at the old `i`, but the old invariant only covered indices up to `i-2`. Thus when `min_price` becomes `prices[i]`, it may not be `<= prices[i-1]`.",
  "repair": "invariant forall j :: 0 <= j < i ==> min_price <= prices[j]"
}
